{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jzt2UoMYET4GtpLyvQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the draft. It's about 150 words, and every claim in it comes from what you told me.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Your own regular cleaner, and $99 to come back\n\nHi [First name],\n\nLast year, one of the complaints we heard most was about a different cleaner showing up each time. That was a fair complaint, and we've fixed it.\n\nSince July, every Brightway customer has their own regular cleaner who gets to know their home. You'll also have a named backup, someone you know ahead of time, for sick days and holidays. Nobody you haven't met will turn up at your door.\n\nIt's working. Since July, only 1 of our 18 cleaners has left.\n\nWe know we cost more than the app services, and here's why. Our cleaners are employees, not contractors. We pay them $21 an hour, and every visit is insured.\n\nTo make it easy to give us another try, your first cleaning back is $99. Just reply to this email or call 555-0164 before December 31.\n\nWarmly,\nLisa Grant\nOwner, Brightway Home Cleaning\n</final_document>\n\nA few notes:\n\n- **What I left out:** The email doesn't say what customers will pay after the $99 visit, because you haven't decided yet. Once you do, add one line saying what regular visits cost. People who left over price will want to know before they book, and they'll trust you more if you tell them up front.\n- **\"Nobody you haven't met\":** This line only holds if the backup is actually introduced to the customer. If you just give them a name, change it to \"Nobody you weren't told about will turn up at your door.\"\n- **The old cleaner's name:** If your system can tell you who each customer's old cleaner was, and that person still works for you, add a line like \"Maria is still with us and would love to come back.\" That would be the strongest line in the email.\n- **[First name]:** This needs a ma